---
import updates from "../../captures/updates.png";
import Callout from "../../guide/Callout.astro";
import GuidePage from "../../guide/GuidePage.astro";
import Path from "../../guide/Path.astro";
import Task from "../../guide/Task.astro";
---

<GuidePage
  slug="library-updates"
  lead="Katari checks your sources for new chapters, episodes and books, either when you ask or on a schedule you set."
>
  <Task id="check" title="Check for new chapters" shot={{ image: updates, alt: "New episodes listed in the updates feed", caption: "Updates" }}>
    <ul>
      <li>Pull down on the library to check the page you're on, such as one category.</li>
      <li>The library's <strong>⋮</strong> menu has <strong>Update library</strong> for everything.</li>
      <li>Pull down on the <strong>Updates</strong> tab to check the whole library.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>What's new lands in <strong>Updates</strong>, newest first.</p>
  </Task>

  <Task id="schedule" title="Check on a schedule">
    <ol>
      <li>Open <Path>Settings › Library updates</Path>.</li>
      <li>Under <strong>Schedule</strong>, set <strong>Automatic updates</strong> to how often to check. It is <strong>Off</strong> at first.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Automatic updates device restrictions</strong> keeps the checks to Wi-Fi, which is how it starts, or to unmetered networks
        or charging.
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p>The top of the screen says when the next check runs and how many titles it will look at.</p>
  </Task>

  <Task id="what-is-checked" title="Choose what gets checked">
    <p>Every check follows the same rules, set on the same screen:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Categories</strong> and <strong>Sources</strong> turn whole categories or sources off.</li>
      <li><strong>Types</strong> leaves out comics, video or books, once your library holds more than one kind.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Skip an entry when…</strong> skips titles that are completed, that you haven't started, or that still have unseen items, and
        checks others only near their expected release. Skipping completed titles and checking near the release are on from the start.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      One title can step out of the rules: on its page, tap the <strong>Updates</strong> button and choose <strong>Always check</strong> or
      <strong>Never check</strong>. <strong>Follow library rules</strong> puts it back. The same sheet says why the title was or wasn't checked.
    </p>
  </Task>

  <Task id="report" title="See what the last check did">
    <p>
      Tap <strong>Last update</strong> in <Path>Settings › Library updates</Path>, or the time at the top of Updates, for the
      <strong>Update report</strong>: what failed, what was new, and what was skipped. Retry or migrate failed titles from there.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Pause source</strong> takes a struggling source out of updates for a day, three days, a week, or until you resume it. Tap it
      again to resume.
    </p>
  </Task>

  <Task id="large-updates" title="Why Katari warns about large updates">
    <p>
      Checking or downloading a lot from one source at once looks like an attack to many sites, and they answer by slowing down or
      blocking requests, sometimes for everyone using the source. Katari warns when one update checks more than 60 titles from a source,
      or when many downloads from one source queue up.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Split your library into categories and turn off the ones you don't follow closely.</li>
      <li>Leave <strong>Only check near its expected release</strong> on.</li>
      <li>Download a few chapters at a time rather than whole series.</li>
    </ul>
    <Callout label="Not a bug">
      <p>The warning only advises; the update or download still runs.</p>
    </Callout>
  </Task>

  <Task id="upcoming" title="What Upcoming shows">
    <p>
      <Path>Updates › View Upcoming Updates</Path> opens a calendar of when titles are expected to get something new, worked out from how
      often they did before. It's an estimate, not a release date: a series on break or a source with wrong dates throws it off.
    </p>
    <p>
      Titles that automatic updates won't check are marked <strong>Won't be checked</strong>, with the reason. <strong>Filter</strong> limits
      the calendar to some categories.
    </p>
  </Task>
</GuidePage>
